  "description": "YIBMAZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C138 H130 N11 Na2 O49 Tb6 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),15(H2 O1),C2 H6 O1. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.773-5.386 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.67-174.57°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Na2Tb6L8(C6H4NH2COO)2(C2H5OH)2(H2O)4(NO3)]·NO3·C2H5OH·14H2O (paper EA C142H177Tb6N13Na2O75; CCDC lattice water 15H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
